  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The pendulum – into the slot and a long shot",
  "description": "Two lines out on each side, just above the centre line, and a goalkeeper. The players in line A have two balls each. B runs diagonally in towards the slot, gets the pass from A and shoots first time. Right after, A takes a long shot, then runs diagonally into the slot and gets the pass from C, who is now first in line B. A shoots first time. The goalkeeper has to keep moving sideways.\n\nRotation: change lines after your shot and run it mirrored so both sides get trained. Harder variant: put a cone beside the goal. After the first shot B rounds it, gets a pass from their own line and shoots first time again – only then does A take the long shot. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Show with your stick where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The pass should be well placed, in front of the runner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Full speed in the runs into the slot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Hit the target – make the goalkeeper work."
    }
  ],
